# YAML 1.2
---
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Bug Connectome Project (Insectome)"
message: >-
  If you use this software or studio in research, please cite it using the
  metadata below, and cite the upstream connectome / morphology datasets you
  actually analyzed (hemibrain, MANC, optic lobe, CREMI, IBdb, etc.).
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Insectome contributors
    website: "https://github.com/theworker02"
  - name: "theworker02"
    website: "https://github.com/theworker02"
repository-code: "https://github.com/theworker02/new-connectome-project"
url: "https://theworker02.github.io/new-connectome-project/"
repository-artifact: "https://github.com/theworker02/bug-connectome-project"
abstract: >-
  Bug Connectome Project (product name: Insectome) is a local multi-species
  insect connectome studio. It federates provenance-tracked packs from public
  sources (neuPrint, CREMI, Insect Brain Database), prioritizes LEVEL-0/1 reuse
  over re-segmentation, streams EM remotely under a bounded cache, and ships a
  static GitHub Pages snapshot for browsing catalogs and sparse morphology.
keywords:
  - connectomics
  - insect
  - Drosophila
  - neuPrint
  - morphology
  - synaptic graph
  - provenance
  - streaming EM
license: MIT
version: "0.4.0"
date-released: "2026-09-24"
identifiers:
  - type: url
    value: "https://github.com/theworker02/new-connectome-project"
    description: Primary implementation repository
  - type: url
    value: "https://github.com/theworker02/bug-connectome-project"
    description: Bug Connectome Project public project identity
preferred-citation:
  type: software
  title: "Bug Connectome Project (Insectome)"
  authors:
    - family-names: Insectome contributors
  version: "0.4.0"
  year: 2026
  url: "https://github.com/theworker02/new-connectome-project"
  notes: >-
    Always cite upstream data sources used for figures or analyses. This software
    citation covers the studio and tooling only.
